id: pm-23xkss
title: "GH-814: SDK metadata reads must distinguish missing and invalid tracker roots from an empty tracker"
description: "Public SDK metadata enumeration silently returns an empty corpus when the supplied tracker root is absent or a regular file. This turns a path error into confident but false project context for graph, search, governance, and extension consumers."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: "area:sdk","area:storage",context-integrity,error-contract
created_at: "2026-07-29T21:43:32.888Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T22:44:18.383Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T22:19:58.359Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T22:19:58.359Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: listAllItemMetadata and its light and body variants reject missing roots and non-directory roots with stable typed diagnostics; a valid empty tracker remains a successful empty result; CLI query and governance callers preserve their intended domain-level errors; public SDK types documentation focused regression tests and installed-consumer acceptance cover the contract
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make foundational SDK reads fail loudly when their source of truth does not exist
value: Agents and extensions never mistake an invalid workspace path for a real project with zero work
impact: "Prevents silent empty graphs, missing blockers, and incorrect release decisions across every SDK consumer"
why_now: GH-814 demonstrates the ambiguity in the current published SDK and an external graph package already needs this contract
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Validated tracker roots before metadata enumeration with stable typed missing and non-directory diagnostics.
expected_result: Empty valid trackers return an empty corpus while invalid or unreadable roots cannot masquerade as project truth.
actual_result: "All three metadata readers preserve empty success, distinguish missing and invalid roots, and rethrow unrelated filesystem errors."
affected_version: 2026.7.29
component: sdk/storage/item-store
regression: true
