comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T21:43:32.888Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence 2026-07-29: searched all 2,197 live items across every status for GH-814, listAllItemMetadata, missing metadata root, nonexistent pm root, regular-file tracker root, empty graph, and SDK reader semantics. No item owns this failure mode. Closed SDK-first and graph primitives establish the affected lineage but do not distinguish invalid roots from an empty valid tracker. GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/814"
  "2026-07-29T22:19:19.094Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: all public metadata enumeration variants now accept an existing empty directory but throw stable typed diagnostics for missing and non-directory roots, while preserving unrelated filesystem errors. Focused tests pass 3/3 and full coverage passes 6540/6540 at 100/100/100/100. A packed SDK consumer proved empty returns [] and missing reports tracker_root_missing with reason missing."
  "2026-07-29T22:29:52.730Z","harness:codex","Delivery review: PR #818 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/818 carries typed empty/missing/non-directory tracker-root semantics, SDK documentation, focused tests, full coverage, and isolated packed-consumer proof. GitHub issue #814 is configured to close on merge."
  "2026-07-29T22:44:18.382Z","harness:codex","Review-loop finding: CodeRabbit correctly identified ENOTDIR when a metadata root traverses beneath a regular file. The typed tracker_root_not_directory mapping and regression coverage now include both a direct file root and file/child traversal."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T22:19:19.795Z","harness:codex",An empty item array is project truth only after the SDK proves the supplied tracker root is an existing directory; filesystem discovery failures must remain distinguishable and non-ENOENT errors must retain their original identity.
